By 4 October, the desk had merged **412 reports** into #4471 and marked the ticket known. The
export separates those reports into two problems: a shared parser that treats dates as month-first,
and a `booking-v3` form hint that conflicts with day-first date handling.

## Problems found

<IncidentSummary />

### Shared parser reads dates month first

**379 reports.** The shared parser treats dates as month-first in day-first tenant locales. This
can swap the day and month before a booking or calendar invite is produced. The affected paths
include app, email, and `booking-v2` forms.

<p><a href={issueUrls.parser}>Open the shared parser issue</a>.</p>

### `booking-v3` form hint conflicts with day-first handling

**33 reports.** The form displays `MM/DD/YYYY` for day-first tenant locales, while it interprets
the submitted value in day-first order. People following the hint can get a flipped date.

<p><a href={issueUrls.hint}>Open the booking-v3 form hint issue</a>.</p>

## How the groups were counted

Counts include unique reports merged into #4471. The cause comes from tenant locale and booking
form configuration. Browser locale and intake tags are not reliable cause labels.

